  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Serco obligated $992M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 437 awards. Serco average award size is $2.3M, and obligations fell 23.6% year over year. Serco obligations have trended upward and then down across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $773M, FY22 was $873M, FY23 was $1.1B, FY24 was $1.5B, and FY25 was $1.3B. Serco work in FY2026 to date is concentrated with a handful of agencies and markets. Serco received $652M from the Department of Defense and $202M from the Department of Health and Human Services. Serco obligations from the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation were $40.7M, and other buying agencies each recorded smaller obligations. Serco markets are led by Engineering Services at $376M and Computer Systems Design Services at $197M. Serco Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) obligations were $101M, with additional obligations in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $79.3M and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $38.1M. This profile highlights Serco’s FY2026 to date agency and market concentration using reported obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Serco's federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $652M for Serco in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $202M for Serco. The Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation obligated $40.7M for Serco, and remaining top buyers recorded smaller obligations. These agency-level figures show Serco revenues are focused among a few large buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Serco's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Engineering Services obligations for Serco were $376M in FY2026 to date. Computer Systems Design Services obligations for Serco were $197M, and Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) obligations were $101M. Serco also recorded obligations in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $79.3M and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $38.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
